# Metropolis line-ending policy — BUG-004.
#
# Module key: foundation.repo (see code.json)
# Spec ref:   M0-ENG §5 ("main is always green")
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Without it, line endings are decided by whatever
# each machine's core.autocrlf happens to be. This repo's blobs are LF,
# but GitHub's windows-latest runners check out with core.autocrlf=true,
# so every .go file arrived in the runner's working directory as CRLF —
# and gofmt reports CRLF files as unformatted. That is why CI's gofmt
# check failed on EVERY run from the very first commit (5faf2ed) while
# `gofmt -l .` stayed clean on every developer machine: the divergence
# between local and CI *was* the bug, so no amount of local checking
# could ever have found it.
#
# Pinning eol=lf makes the checked-out bytes identical everywhere, which
# is the only state in which "gofmt is clean locally" is evidence about
# CI at all.
#
# Do not "fix" this by relaxing the gofmt check. The check was right.

# Default: normalise all text to LF in the repo and in every working
# directory, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Go tooling requires LF; state it explicitly so the intent survives any
# future edit to the default line above.
*.go     text eol=lf
*.mod    text eol=lf
*.sum    text eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the genuine exception: cmd.exe can mis-parse
# LF-only .bat/.cmd, so these keep CRLF deliberately.
*.bat    text eol=crlf
*.cmd    text eol=crlf

# Binary assets — never touch these.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.gz     binary
*.exe    binary
